# Trivy ignore file
# Format: CVE-ID or vulnerability ID
# Add comments with #
#
# Populate this file as Trivy findings are triaged. Entries must include a
# comment justifying the suppression. Do not add entries without triage.
#
# Hard gate policy (see .github/workflows/security.yml): trivy fails the
# pipeline on CRITICAL findings only. HIGH findings are surfaced in the
# GitHub Security tab (SARIF) for triage and are expected to shrink as
# dependabot bumps the vendored tree.

# CVE-2026-33186 (google.golang.org/grpc authorization bypass, fixed in 1.79.3):
# grpc appears only in vendored module metadata - github.com/tjfoc/gmsm and
# github.com/xtaci/kcp-go/v5 declare it in their go.mod/go.sum but no Go
# source in this tree imports google.golang.org/grpc, so the vulnerable code
# is never compiled. Re-check if gmsm/kcp-go are ever upgraded to import it.
CVE-2026-33186
